      "status_notes": "CVE-2026-114583: tarfile.tar_filter could be bypassed with crafted link entries, including symlinks with empty or directory-like names, so tarfile.extractall() with filter='tar' could write files outside the destination directory. Upstream fixed it in https://github.com/python/cpython/issues/160097 (3.14 commit https://github.com/python/cpython/commit/0901ad4ffb22605f12b705d1c1197f0a01f0ba0b), first released in CPython 3.14.10; see https://mail.python.org/archives/list/security-announce@python.org/thread/43JOWPRAV5DI3VZ4FUEUAZOHCATXXOCK/; https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-114583. Compared Lib/tarfile.py in every published build, 3.14.3-r0 to 3.14.10-r4, of the DHI Alpine 3.23 python-3.14 package on x86_64 and aarch64 with the files in the upstream CPython 3.14 releases. 3.14.3-r0 to 3.14.8-r1 lack the fix; 3.14.10-r0 is the first published build that has it and is built from the upstream 3.14.10 release, and every later build carries it."
